       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Two policy/legislative initiative aimed at better managing diaspora investment potential 
- One major policy proposal developed: Carta Serbica - is a program intended for individuals from the Serbian diaspora who do not hold Serbian citizenship and are interested in living, working or retiring in Serbia. Following the initiative by the Returning Point, a streamlined procedure for obtaining temporary residence and work permits was introduced, specially designed for foreigners of Serbian origin. 
- The Returning Point was conceived to support circular migrations, secure contact with highly qualified migrants, and lead to new labour market policies for immigrants and a more inviting environment for returnees. The Returning Point has crystalized into a team with the mission to establish and maintain networks and to build bridges between Serbian society at home and abroad through various programs. The initiation Plan of the UNDP has helped to pilot the platform, and in October 2021, the Returning Point was established as a non-governmental organization. The first grant has been provided to the organization. The key purpose of the grant was to create a better environment for the repatriation of the diaspora and cooperation between Serbian society at home and abroad. 
-Through UNDP procedures, the project support staff for this Project has been established and fully operational.</narrative>
